# The file system at its edges (roadmap os-server.md P15, the second
# review): init starts tests/posix/edges.c (TEST_POSIX_EDGES), which fills
# B but three clusters; a byte written past a hole of ten clusters into an
# empty file is ENOSPC, and gives back the clusters it took (before, it
# kept them: lost, and the next 3 KB found no room); then the root is
# filled with empty files, and a rename in it takes no slot (before,
# ENOSPC). fsck.fat finds B sound after.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_EDGES
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
fsck: B
timeout: 300
emulators: bochs
---
edges: B full, then 3 clusters freed (0): 0
edges: a byte past a hole of 10 clusters (-1, ENOSPC 28): -1, errno 28
edges: its size after (0): 0
edges: then 3 KB in another file (3072): 3072
edges: the root full (ENOSPC 28): 28
edges: a rename in it (0): 0
edges: done
